1
00:00:57,115 --> 00:01:06,113
Good morning everyone and welcome to the Annual Ski and Snowboard Exhibition held from April 8th to 17th.

2
00:01:06,113 --> 00:01:09,808
I am Mary Granger, coordinator of the event this year.


3
00:01:09,808 --> 00:01:12,399
The 10-day event features many highlights.

4
00:01:12,389 --> 00:01:17,208
As a snow sports lover, I know you are looking forward to a great time here.

5
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:23,900
Now I’d like to offer you some practical information about the whole event and what to expect from it.

6
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,859
This might be the first time coming here for some of you.

7
00:01:27,859 --> 00:01:33,266
So for those who are still wondering about the right accommodation, I recommend Sky Hotel.

8
00:01:33,266 --> 00:01:46,107
It has its own health and sports clubs just like most of the hotels here, but I love it because of its incredibly cozy beds which guarantees good rest after an exhausting day of exploration.

9
00:01:46,107 --> 00:01:56,793
If you haven’t brought your own equipment, like poles, boots and skis, they are available for purchase or rent at Ski Set or Snow Rental.

10
00:01:56,793 --> 00:02:05,942
The exhibition this year provides a colorful look into the history of skiing and an inspiring peek into the future prospects of the sport.

11
00:02:05,942 --> 00:02:11,530
Apart from the fascinating photo exhibitions and the most up-to-date skiing gear like always. 

12
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:24,839
This year we have added four computers which can imitate the process of skiing, ensuring the same physical activity and sensations that appear during the skiing process on downhill slopes.

13
00:02:24,839 --> 00:02:31,017
But I have to warn you that it might be quite time-consuming to line up for the free trial experience.


14
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:36,387
Many have posed the question as to how to enter the skiing and snowboarding competition.

15
00:02:36,387 --> 00:02:49,158
Well, rather than filling out the back of the entrance ticket or bombarding the committee with emails, the most effective method is by checking out the exhibition newsletter delivered every month for availability.


16
00:02:49,158 --> 00:02:54,714
As the most beloved local event, the exhibition has also drawn attention from the press.

17
00:02:54,714 --> 00:02:59,612
Last year, massive media coverage was on the worrisome amount
of snowfall.


18
00:02:59,612 --> 00:03:05,224
In order to avoid the same predicament, several artificial skiing slopes have been built.


19
00:03:05,224 --> 00:03:12,195
With more participants this year, we have lowered the entrance fee which has been widely reported by local newspapers.


20
00:03:12,195 --> 00:03:15,636
A bonus for our participants is the ski program. 

21
00:03:15,636 --> 00:03:26,943
It offers a wide variety of lessons and sessions with qualified instructors ensuring that all ages and abilities are catered to from the first timers to seasoned amateurs.


22
00:03:26,943 --> 00:03:34,876
I strongly advise you to sign up for the program as it is offering an unprecedented 30% discount.


23
00:03:34,876 --> 00:03:44,450
That’s mainly because we are cooperating with the program organiser who promises affordable prices only for the participants of the festival this year.


24
00:04:20,384 --> 00:04:28,310
Now I would like to introduce to you the list of presentations during the following week so that you can better plan your schedule.


25
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:32,979
The first presenter Simon is one of our best ski instructors. 

26
00:04:32,969 --> 00:04:39,363
As an experienced instructor, he will inform you about the dangers that face skiers and snowboarders. 

27
00:04:39,363 --> 00:04:44,034
Accidents happen mostly to those who are careless or ignorant.

28
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:49,533
Good risk management involves considering both the probability and consequences of an accident.

29
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:54,698
The next speech titled Solution is given by Jamie Kurt. 

30
00:04:54,698 --> 00:05:08,862
A list of problems may occur to novice skiers and snowboarders, so he is going to offer useful information for first timers on choosing the appropriate gears, the right dress code and ways of protecting your skin.

31
00:05:08,862 --> 00:05:16,314
For instance, some of you may have rented the skiing equipment, but rental footwear is notoriously uncomfortable.

32
00:05:16,314 --> 00:05:21,643
Then Jamie will provide instructions to help make your footwear fit better.


33
00:05:21,643 --> 00:05:29,643
The third speech is about a documentary introducing skiing and snowboarding and the difference between the two sports.

34
00:05:29,643 --> 00:05:35,932
It also depicts a group of snow lovers exploring new slopes with breath-taking views.


35
00:05:35,932 --> 00:05:40,688
The director Andy Fisher will be there, addressing the whole shooting experience.


36
00:05:40,688 --> 00:05:45,548
The fourth talk is about the tricks of skiing, presented by Harry Tyson.

37
00:05:45,548 --> 00:05:51,857
It is most useful for those who have already tried skiing, yet still need more practice to master the sport.


38
00:05:51,857 --> 00:05:55,076
Harry will teach you how to turn more skillfully.

39
00:05:55,076 --> 00:06:03,341
A lot of people can keep their skis roughly parallel but there’s no point if you make it hard to work with and slide around out of control.

40
00:06:03,341 --> 00:06:12,251
Useful exercises will also be suggested to improve your parallel skiing technique so that you can tackle steeper slopes and enjoy yourself more.


41
00:06:12,251 --> 00:06:21,032
Johnson Smith will be the last presenter, mainly addressing towards advanced skiers. He manages to apply snow climbing into skiing.

42
00:06:21,032 --> 00:06:24,620
Climbing in soft snow, you are floundering around.

43
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:34,741
Walking becomes harder, so a good trick during climbing is to maintain a wider gait, approximately shoulder width, so that you are more stable while walking.

44
00:06:34,741 --> 00:06:36,633
This works for skiing as well.